87	153,615,209,948	87. Linear.	Outline of a narrow leaf many times longer than wide, of about the same width from base to rounded tip, with a single midrib.
88	249,615,335,948	88. Lance-shaped.	Outline of a narrow leaf much longer than wide, tapering to a sharp point above and more gently below, with fine veins off the midrib.
89	380,620,536,946	89. Oblong.	Outline of a leaf two or three times longer than broad, with nearly straight parallel sides and rounded ends, feather-veined.
90	563,619,752,948	90. Oval.	Outline of a broad leaf with a smooth, flowing elliptical outline, rounded at both ends, feather-veined from the midrib.
91	771,620,979,948	91. Ovate.	Outline of an egg-shaped leaf, broadest towards the lower end and narrowing to a blunt point, feather-veined.
92	1004,619,1268,944	92. Heart-shaped.	Outline of a broad, pointed leaf with a toothed margin and a little notch at the base where the stalk joins, feather-veined.
93	1346,618,1614,948	93. Orbicular.	Outline of a nearly circular leaf with a small notch at the stalk, its veins curving out from the base.
94	971,1300,1055,1640	94. Oblanceolate.	Outline of a narrow leaf shaped like a lance with the point downwards, broadest above and tapering to the stalk.
95	1087,1307,1192,1640	95. Spatulate.	Outline of a leaf rounded at the top and tapering into a long, narrow base, like a spatula.
96	1223,1297,1424,1640	96. Obovate.	Outline of an egg-shaped leaf with the narrow end at the bottom, broad and rounded above, feather-veined.
97	1455,1305,1648,1636	97. Cuneate or Wedge-shaped.	Outline of a leaf broad and rounded at the top, its sides narrowing in straight lines down to a point at the base, like a wedge.
